# Input
```
-- A temporal unique constraint (Postgres 18) needs a GiST index, so USING INDEX is no alternative
-- expect_lint/disallowUniqueConstraint
ALTER TABLE bookings ADD CONSTRAINT bookings_room_key UNIQUE (room_id, during WITHOUT OVERLAPS);

```

# Diagnostics
lint/disallowUniqueConstraint ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Adding a UNIQUE constraint requires an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock.
  
  i There is no concurrent alternative for a temporal key (WITHOUT OVERLAPS). Use SET lock_timeout to limit the impact on concurrent operations.
